// Title: Domain Trust Discovery Via Dsquery
// Sigma ID: 3bad990e-4848-4a78-9530-b427d854aac0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: E.M. Anhaus, Tony Lambert, oscd.community, omkar72
// Date: 2019-10-24 | Modified: 2023-02-02
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1482
// Description: Detects execution of "dsquery.exe" for domain trust discovery
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the utilities by legitimate user for legitimate reason
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1482/T1482.md
//   - https://posts.specterops.io/an-introduction-to-manual-active-directory-querying-with-dsquery-and-ldapsearch-84943c13d7eb?gi=41b97a644843
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dsquery_domain_trust_discovery.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\dsquery.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "dsquery.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "trustedDomain"
